rtnership with Vans. \"This meant booking fishbone, the muddy, muddy boss tones, no effect, 3-11 penny wise, and this weird new group from San Diego called Blink 182.\"","year":1996,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"24 Years of the Warped Tour","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7jfQaUV6Bq4"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Long-Running Career on Epitaph","body":"NOFX had been active since 1983 and had consistently released records on Epitaph Records since 1989, making them a well-established presence in the punk scene before their 1994 breakthrough. \"No effects who had been around since 1983 and had been releasing records on Epitaphs since 1989.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The 90s Part 6: The Punk Revival","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0QtMI00T5jw"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"MTV Video Policy","body":"NoFX had a strict policy against allowing MTV to play their music videos, which likely prevented them from achieving even greater mainstream success during the 1990s punk rock revival. \"No Effects had a policy of not letting MTV play their videos.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Alt Rock Revivals Part 1: Punk","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gkLMwrthZ9s"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Sex Toy Line (Unspecified Year)","body":"NOFX is among the rock acts that have released their own line of sex toys, specifically an inflatable sheep. \"No Effects, which is an inflatable sheep, if you must ask\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Tales of Weird Rock’n’Roll Sex","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DA2iJsu3GRY"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Still Active","body":"Led by singer Fat Mike, NOFX remains a \"going concern\" in the music industry today. \"No effects led by singer Fatmouk, still a going concern today.\"","year":null,"extra"